new file mode 100644
index 0000000..6c24390
--- /dev/null
+++ b/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@
+# Daily Grind WebMCP
+
+The homepage exposes three client-side tools through native WebMCP:
+
+| Tool | Input | Effect |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `get_seasonal_menu` | Optional `query` string | Searches the visible Seasonal Favorites names and descriptions; returns drink ids and details without changing the page. |
+| `select_drink` | Required `drinkId` | Highlights the drink, updates the dropdown, and focuses the order section. |
+| `order_drink` | Required `drinkId`; optional integer `quantity` (1–10, default 1) | Adds an entry to the visible demo order list and announces confirmation. Each call adds another entry. |
+
+Drink ids: `maple-oat-latte`, `dark-roast-espresso`, `cold-brew`. For example, an agent can call `order_drink` with `{"drinkId":"maple-oat-latte","quantity":2}`. Tool results contain JSON in a text content block; invalid inputs return `isError: true` with a corrective message.
+
+Orders exist only in the current page's memory and reset on reload. They do not charge money, contact a café, or imply fulfillment. The menu cards, form, live confirmation, and order list work without WebMCP support.
+
+`webmcp.js` registers with `document.modelContext` when available, falling back to the earlier `navigator.modelContext` API. It does not install a polyfill or start an MCP server. Native agent discovery requires a WebMCP-capable browser with the feature enabled in a secure context. See the [Chrome WebMCP API guide](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/modern-web-guidance/guides/webmcp/agentic-javascript-tools) for current browser requirements and registration details.
+
+Run `npm test` for Node tests using DOM and registration doubles. These cover registration, querying, shared UI actions, input validation, cancellation, unsupported browsers, and registration failures; they do not launch a browser or server. This static project has no build step.
